{%- set v = hosted.values -%}
{%- set saved -%}
{%- for f in ["host", "username", "password"] if hosted.vars[f] %}`{{ hosted.vars[f] }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- endset -%}
{%- if hosted.vendor == "neon" -%}
Create a Neon project for the stack's databases. The script needs
[`neonctl`](https://neon.tech/docs/reference/neon-cli), signed in (`neonctl auth`, or
`NEON_API_KEY` set), and `jq`. It creates the project `trestle-{{ env_name }}` unless it exists
(in `NEON_REGION`, default `aws-us-east-2`), then saves its id as `NEON_PROJECT_ID`
{%- if saved %} and its connection details as {{ saved }}{% endif %} in `secrets.env`.
{%- elif hosted.vendor == "aws-rds" -%}
Create an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL instance. The script needs the AWS CLI, signed in to the
account (a profile, SSO, or keys), and `openssl`. It creates the instance `trestle-{{ env_name }}`
unless it exists (in `AWS_REGION`, default `us-east-1`; class `RDS_INSTANCE_CLASS`, default
`db.t4g.micro`), with a generated password unless one is set, waits until it is available, and
saves {{ saved or "its connection details" }} in `secrets.env`.

The instance is publicly accessible in the account's default VPC, so the stack can reach it from
your machine. Allow inbound TCP 5432 from your address in its security group, and nothing wider.
{%- elif hosted.vendor == "azure-postgres" -%}
Create an Azure Database for PostgreSQL flexible server. The script needs the Azure CLI, signed
in (`az login`), `openssl`, and `AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP` set to an existing resource group. It
creates the server `AZURE_POSTGRES_SERVER` (default `trestle-{{ env_name }}`; the name must be
unique across Azure) unless it exists, in `AZURE_LOCATION` (default `eastus`), with a generated
password unless one is set. The firewall admits `AZURE_POSTGRES_ALLOW_IP`, by default this
machine's public address. It then saves {{ saved or "its connection details" }} in `secrets.env`.
{%- else -%}
Provide a PostgreSQL server the stack can reach from where it runs (port {{ v.port }}), and a
role that may create databases. The stack connects to `{{ v.host }}` as `{{ v.username }}`
{%- if v.ssl_mode %} with `sslmode={{ v.ssl_mode }}`{% endif %}. Set {{ saved or "the connection's variables" }} to match.
{%- endif %}
